  "question": {
    "text": "A ball having kinetic energy KE, is projected at an angle of $60^{\\circ}$ from the horizontal. What will be the kinetic energy of ball at the highest point of its flight ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "OHALB",
      "text": "$\\frac{(\\mathrm{KE})}{8}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bVx9W",
      "text": "$\\frac{(\\mathrm{KE})}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pzbtC",
      "text": "$\\frac{(\\mathrm{KE})}{16}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sWjiL",
      "text": "$\\frac{(\\mathrm{KE})}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Initial K.E,\n$\\text { K.E. }=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{mu}^2$\n\nSpeed at heighest point\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{V}=\\mathrm{u} \\cos 60^{\\circ}=\\frac{\\mathrm{u}}{2} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{KE}_2=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{~m}\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{u}}{2}\\right)^2 \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{4} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{mu}^2 \\\\\n& =\\frac{\\mathrm{KE}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
